\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Look, Ye Saints! The sight is glorious,
\par See the Man of Sorrows now,
\par From the fight returned victorious;
\par Every knee to Him shall bow.
\par Crown Him! Crown Him! 
\par Crowns become the Victor's brow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Crown the Saviour, angels crown Him:
\par Rich the trophies Jesus brings;
\par In the seat of power enthrone Him,
\par Crown Him! Crown Him! 
\par Crown the Saviour, King of kings.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Sinners in derision crowned Him,
\par Mocking thus the Saviour's claim;
\par Saints and angels crowd around Him,
\par Own His title, praise His name.
\par Crown Him! Crown Him! 
\par Spread abroad the Victor's fame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Hark, those bursts of acclamation;
\par Hark, those loud triumphant chords;
\par Jesus takes the highest station:
\par O what joy the sight affords!
\par Crown Him! Crown Him! 
\par King of kings, and Lord of lords!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

